[Applause]  do you ever wonder where protesters come  from after the Prime Minister prorogued  Parliament they were everywhere from  London to Manchester how did they find  each other and how'd you get them to  turnout  even in the rain the answer can be found  here at the home of Mike Goldsworthy  founder of popular remain campaign  scientists for EU for the last seven  months he's been secretly working with  local remain activists to help them  build support on Facebook we've worked  with over a hundred local pages now and  spent over a hundred thousand pounds in  tools in one-on-one help and also in  advertising directly for those pages we  have quadrupled the amount of people  following local pro you pages with  dozens and dozens of pages where they  were small ineffectual pages before  they've really come alive and built a  community and that is fuelled the  on-the-ground community as well  politics on Facebook is hardly new but  what I've just seen marks a definite  shift on the remain side people are  moving from amateur to professional and  whether you like it or not that is how  modern political campaigns are won and  lost these are the local remains  Facebook pages Mike's working on one  hundred and sixteen of them he says  they're now beating their leave  equivalents in almost every area of the  country although social media experts  are skeptical the results are impressive  but the problem is it doesn't really  give a full spectrum of people's beliefs  a lot of people on the leave side won't  necessarily engage in this sort of  content on social media they're much  more like the shy Tory type of people so  they sort of are passive on social media  they see things they don't really  comment they don't really like rose on  the remain side it's a lot more vocal  still the network's having an impact as  this protest in Cheltenham shows it was  arranged on Niki Robson's Facebook page  which six months ago had just 130  followers now  now Nicky can call on 4000 followers to  protest her local MP you know come with  us tomorrow lunchtime and let's have a  conversation with him about what his  views are on what's taking place so  within 24 hours we arrived at his office  and there were around 300 individuals  from from his constituency so now you  know a lot of protesters come from  Facebook as MPs debate this week  remember the fight online could be just  as crucial role and mantle Sky News

